Subject: CPMS I02C Canonical Document and Golden Bundle Semantic Refinement

@ [refinement_uuid] 27c347d2-ce93-4d92-bd7f-7b66cdab492b

& [RootDraft] is generator structure without released closure
& [CanonicalDocument] is one root plus exact same-direction closure, stable dialect and id, normalized bytes, account, and digest
& [BundlePayload] is the five documents plus two direction-qualified inventories and generation metadata before its own digest exists
& [GoldenBundle] is payload plus recomputable bundle digest and exact-baseline fingerprint
& [GoldenArtifact] is a checked-in byte projection of one canonical document or bundle envelope and grants no authority beyond the signed generation contract

& [SchemaMetadata] stays outside JSON Schema vocabulary
  + the schema value contains standard $schema, $id, structural keywords, and local $defs
  + direction, root kind, generator, source revision, fingerprints, accounts, and residual ids live in the document record and bundle manifest
  + no provider-private or Cantor-private schema keyword is introduced

& [ResponseIdentity] is intended-use preserving
  + base_response and preparation_response begin with equal raw roots today
  + their different stable $id values make their canonical document bytes and digests different
  + equality before $id insertion is recorded as structural evidence and never used as substitution authority

& [BaselineSignature] is content identity only
  + it is a domain-separated fingerprint over the bundle digest and ordered document identities and digests
  + it is not a keyed digital signature, signer recognition, semantic compatibility proof, or authority admission
  + exact replay may be classified identical; any change remains unclassified and blocking for later compatibility work

& [SourceRevision] names generation input
  + generated artifacts may be committed after the source revision they bind
  + the containing commit is lineage metadata and does not rewrite generated bytes
